## 6. Filtering & Hybrid Search

### Q: Why is filtered vector search hard?

HNSW doesn't know about your filter columns. Two flawed options:

| Approach | Works when | Fails when |
|---|---|---|
| **Post-filter** (search then filter) | Filter is loose (>50% survives) | Filter is strict — might not get K results |
| **Pre-filter** (filter then search) | Filter is very selective (<1%) — brute-force the subset | Middle-selectivity filters — HNSW index unusable on arbitrary subset |

Middle-selectivity is where DBs differ.

### Q: How do the big DBs handle filtering?

| DB | Approach |
|---|---|
| **pgvector** | Planner picks vector index OR filter index — either/or, no filtered HNSW |
| **Elasticsearch** | Applies filter **during** HNSW traversal — guaranteed K results, slower for strict filters |
| **Pinecone** | Inverted indexes on metadata, intersected with vector search in one op |

### Q: What is hybrid search?

**Keyword search (BM25) + vector search**, merged. Query "red running shoes" uses keyword for "red" and vector for semantic breadth. Common ranking function: reciprocal rank fusion. Different from filtered search.

