## 7. Writes & Index Maintenance

### Q: Are vector DBs read-heavy?

**Yes.** Typical read:write ratio is 100:1 to 10,000:1. HNSW build is expensive; graph degrades with continuous writes. Vector DBs assume "write occasionally, read millions of times."

### Q: How do production systems handle writes?

**Hot/cold index pattern:**

```
Query
  ├──> HOT: small index or flat list of recent writes (brute-force OK)
  └──> COLD: big HNSW, rebuilt periodically
  → Merge results
```

Hot merges into cold periodically via full rebuild.

### Q: How are deletes handled?

**Soft deletes** — mark as deleted, filter at query time. Actually removing would require rewiring graph edges. Deleted vectors keep taking space until next rebuild.

### Q: How long do rebuilds take?

| Vector count | Build time |
|---|---|
| 100K | Seconds |
| 1M | Minutes |
| 10M | ~1 hour |
| 100M+ | Many hours |

Survival strategies: rolling rebuild (build new alongside old, swap), partitioned index, background reindex.

