## 8. Which Vector DB to Pick

### Q: Golden rule?

**Start with an extension to a DB you already run.** Purpose-built vector DBs only when scale demands it (~100M+ vectors).

### Q: Tier 1 — Extensions

| Option | When |
|---|---|
| **pgvector** | Already on Postgres. ACID, JOINs, familiar tooling. Handles millions easily. |
| **Elasticsearch kNN** | Already on ES. Best-in-class hybrid search. |
| **Redis Vector** | Need low-latency real-time, Redis already in stack |
| **S3 Vector** | Cold data, already on AWS |

### Q: Tier 2 — Purpose-built (>100M vectors)

| Option | Vibe |
|---|---|
| **Pinecone** | Fully managed, easiest to operate, most expensive |
| **Weaviate** | Open source, GraphQL API, good hybrid search |
| **Milvus** | Built for billions of vectors, distributed = complex |
| **Qdrant** | Rust, excellent filtering — pick if filters are central |
| **Chroma** | Lightweight, RAG prototyping only |

