## 9. Interview Playbook

### Q: When do vector DBs come up?

Almost always AI/ML-adjacent — you'll know in advance. Common patterns:

| Question | Vector DB role |
|---|---|
| Semantic search / doc search | Embed docs, search on query |
| Recommendations | Embed items & users, find similar |
| Reverse image search | CLIP embeddings, similarity search |
| RAG / knowledge Q&A | Retrieve docs, LLM synthesizes |
| Near-duplicate / dedup | Embed items, threshold match |
| Fraud/anomaly detection | Embed transactions, find outliers |

### Q: Default architecture pattern to whiteboard?

```
[Client Query]
    │
    ▼
[Embedding Service] → generate query vector
    │
    ▼
[Vector DB] → return top-K IDs
    │
    ▼
[Primary DB] → fetch full item details
    │
    ▼
[Response]
```

Vector DB is a **specialized index**, not the source of truth.

### Q: Numbers to know

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Typical embedding dims | 128–1536 (OpenAI = 1536) |
| Memory per vector | 4 bytes × dims (1536 dims ≈ 6KB) |
| 1M vectors @ 1536 dims | ~6GB raw, ~12GB with HNSW |
| Query latency (tuned) | 1–10ms |
| Recall target | 95%+ typical, 99%+ expensive |
| Throughput | 10Ks QPS per node (in-memory) |
| Threshold for purpose-built DB | ~100M vectors |

